    {
      "claim": "As of January 1, 2024, the AHV pension can be drawn flexibly starting at age 64.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "You can claim a partial pension as early as age 64.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "For each year you delay claiming beyond age 64, your pension increases by 8.33%.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Maximum pension is payable at age 70.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Full AHV pension remains eligible at age 65 (the traditional retirement age).",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    },
    {
      "claim": "If you delay claiming beyond age 70, there is no further increase; the pension stays at the maximum rate.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    }
  ],
  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant provides incorrect information about the flexible pension age (claims it starts at 64 instead of 63) and misrepresents key details such as the percentage increase per year of deferral and the maximum pension age, thereby contradicting the reference material and providing potentially misleading information.",
  "evidence": "As of January 1, 2024, the AHV (Alters- und Hinterlassenenversicherung, or Old-Age and Survivors Insurance) pension in Switzerland can be drawn flexibly starting at age 64."
